  "question": {
    "text": "Let $\\alpha$ and $\\beta$ be the sum and the product of all the non-zero solutions of the equation $(\\bar{z})^2+|z|=0$, $z \\in$ C. Then $4\\left(\\alpha^2+\\beta^2\\right)$ is equal to :",
    "image": null
  },
  "options": [
    {
      "id": "SZh1p",
      "text": "6",
      "image": null,
      "isCorrect": false
    },
    {
      "id": "2TWko",
      "text": "8",
      "image": null,
      "isCorrect": false
    },
    {
      "id": "mtqzt",
      "text": "2",
      "image": null,
      "isCorrect": false
    },
    {
      "id": "VDjey",
      "text": "4",
      "image": null,
      "isCorrect": true
    }
  ],
  "correctValue": null,
  "solution": {
    "text": "$\\begin{array}{ll}z=x+i y & \\\\ \\bar{z}=x-i y & \\\\ \\bar{z}^2=x^2-y^2-2 i x y & \\\\ \\Rightarrow x^2-y^2-2 i x y+\\sqrt{x^2+y^2}=0 \\\\ \\Rightarrow x=0 \\quad \\text { or } & y=0 \\\\ -y^2+|y|=0 & x^2+|x|=0 \\\\ |y|=|y|^2 & \\Rightarrow x=0 \\\\ y=0, \\pm 1 & \\Rightarrow \\alpha=i-i=0 \\\\ \\Rightarrow i,-i & \\beta=i(-i)=1 \\\\ \\text { are roots } & 4(0+1)=4\\end{array}$",
    "image": null
  },
